1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,344
We would like to share our
plans to introduce the

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:08,200
new JEI English Online
Adaptive Assessment system.

3
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:12,695
As AI and data-driven
learning become more common,

4
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:15,550
parents expect more than a
simple level assessment.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,749
They want to know where their
children struggle, where

6
00:00:18,798 --> 00:00:21,300
they should start, and how
much they have improved.

7
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:26,087
We aim to improve our assessment
system to provide more

8
00:00:26,142 --> 00:00:29,290
accurate starting points and
personalized learning plans.

9
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:34,675
Major U.S. Adaptive Assessment
programs adjust questions based

10
00:00:34,733 --> 00:00:38,720
on student responses and connect
results with personalized learning.

11
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:44,005
Two common methods are CAT,
or Computerized Adaptive

12
00:00:44,074 --> 00:00:47,010
Testing, and IRT, or Item Response Theory.

13
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:51,905
CAT adjusts questions based on
student responses, while IRT

14
00:00:51,979 --> 00:00:56,840
uses question difficulty and
responses to estimate ability levels.

15
00:00:58,590 --> 00:01:03,230
NWEA MAP Growth tracks student
progress through regular assessments.

16
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:07,040
i-Ready connects assessment results
with personalized learning.

17
00:01:07,490 --> 00:01:11,640
IXL recommends learning activities
based on ongoing assessments.

18
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:15,580
Star Reading focuses on reading
skills and progress tracking.

19
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:19,818
Our goal is to connect
precise assessment with

20
00:01:19,874 --> 00:01:22,350
personalized learning,
as these programs do.

21
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:27,410
Our current JEI English
assessments vary by level.

22
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:31,220
Lower levels focus mainly on
basic reading and Phonics.

23
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:36,550
From Level C to J, Grammar and
Reading become the main areas.

24
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,440
Levels I and J also have
significantly more questions.

25
00:01:41,090 --> 00:01:44,068
We plan to review these
differences and determine how

26
00:01:44,124 --> 00:01:47,270
to apply Adaptive Assessment
to each learning objective.

27
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:53,340
Many JEI English assessment questions
contain several sub-questions.

28
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:56,600
Currently, even one incorrect
sub-question causes

29
00:01:56,657 --> 00:01:59,410
the entire main question
to be marked incorrect.

30
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:04,345
We plan to assess sub-questions
separately and assign

31
00:02:04,405 --> 00:02:07,710
three roles: Initial, Check,
and Final Check Questions.

32
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:10,646
This will help us check understanding more

33
00:02:10,703 --> 00:02:13,430
accurately and identify
specific learning needs.

34
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:18,850
Math and English require different
approaches to Adaptive Assessment.

35
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:22,141
In Math, reducing the number
of questions is a key

36
00:02:22,198 --> 00:02:25,380
goal because long assessments
can cause student fatigue.

37
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:30,390
In English, the main challenge
is confirming understanding.

38
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:34,840
One incorrect answer may not mean a
student does not understand a skill.

39
00:02:36,490 --> 00:02:40,490
Also, English learning objectives do
not always follow a clear sequence.

40
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:43,518
Therefore, we will focus
on checking understanding

41
00:02:43,569 --> 00:02:45,580
through multiple questions when needed.

42
00:02:47,330 --> 00:02:50,140
English skill areas have
different learning structures.

43
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:54,430
Phonics, Decoding, and some Grammar
skills follow a clear sequence.

44
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:58,320
Reading Comprehension skills do
not always follow a fixed order.

45
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:03,640
We will assess skills step by
step where the sequence is clear.

46
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:07,770
For other skills, we will check
each learning objective separately.

47
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:11,774
We will use an Initial
Question and a Check

48
00:03:11,826 --> 00:03:14,080
Question to assess each
learning objective.

49
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:18,390
If both answers are correct, we move
to the next learning objective.

50
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:21,502
If both are incorrect, we
identify the objective

51
00:03:21,557 --> 00:03:23,720
as an area that needs further learning.

52
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:27,370
If the answers are mixed, we
provide a Final Check Question.

53
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:31,885
We will then follow the
learning sequence where it is

54
00:03:31,939 --> 00:03:35,020
clear or assess objectives
independently where it is not.

55
00:03:36,770 --> 00:03:39,570
Our current assessment
has two main limitations.

56
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:44,660
First, it is difficult to distinguish simple
mistakes from a lack of understanding.

57
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:49,670
Second, we have limited data to analyze
question difficulty and response patterns.

58
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:53,607
In the first stage, we will improve how we

59
00:03:53,661 --> 00:03:56,220
use individual responses
and collect more data.

60
00:03:56,670 --> 00:04:00,073
Later, we plan to use methods
such as IRT to improve

61
00:04:00,138 --> 00:04:03,410
assessment accuracy and
analyze incorrect answers.

62
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:08,203
Currently, students complete
fixed assessment questions,

63
00:04:08,257 --> 00:04:10,920
and we assign learning
sets based on the results.

64
00:04:11,370 --> 00:04:15,800
With Adaptive Assessment, we will adjust
questions based on student responses.

65
00:04:17,450 --> 00:04:21,241
We will also expand learning
options to include standard

66
00:04:21,308 --> 00:04:25,370
sets, sets with POD, POD-only
learning, and online learning.

67
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:30,460
In the first stage, we will focus on
standard sets and sets combined with POD.

68
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:34,930
Our Adaptive Assessment
will follow four steps.

69
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:38,250
First, we will identify
possible starting points.

70
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:42,620
Second, we will check understanding
using Initial and Check Questions.

71
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:48,040
Third, we will provide additional
questions when results are unclear.

72
00:04:48,490 --> 00:04:51,133
Finally, we will assign
standard sets or sets

73
00:04:51,191 --> 00:04:54,010
combined with POD based
on each student's needs.

74
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:58,720
This process connects assessment results
directly with personalized learning.

75
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:03,156
We aim to develop an Adaptive
Assessment system that

76
00:05:03,208 --> 00:05:06,100
reflects the unique characteristics
of English learning.

77
00:05:06,550 --> 00:05:10,162
We will improve our existing
assessment questions and connect the

78
00:05:10,218 --> 00:05:13,830
results with personalized learning
through standard sets and POD.

79
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:18,513
In the future, we plan to
use learning data to improve

80
00:05:18,567 --> 00:05:21,500
assessment accuracy and expand
into Adaptive Learning.

81
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:22,810
Thank you.

